    "image_with_text_ifmM4X": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_XV8hWF": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading_text": "Our growers achieve results",
            "heading_size": "h3",
            "enable_h1_tag": false
          }
        },
        "description_qMJUet": {
          "type": "description",
          "settings": {
            "description_text": "<p>When you invest in a truffle orchard, one outcome matters most: <strong>harvesting exceptional truffles and selling them</strong>. American Truffle Company exists to make that happen, and our partner growers have been consistently producing world-class truffles in North America. In 2018, a partner orchard harvested the first scientifically cultivated Périgord black truffle in America using ATC science—a 108-gram gem that was prepared that same night by a Michelin-starred chef. In 2020, the very first Burgundy truffle was harvested, demonstrating that our science works across multiple truffle species. Subsequently, a partner grower achieved a record four-year first harvest of Périgord truffles, with a standout total yield and several truffles weighing over 100 grams. ATC partner orchards continued producing multiple icon-class truffles, including a 412-gram Périgord that a Michelin-starred chef described as a world-class truffle, unmatched in freshness and quality. These are not lucky anecdotes, but the predictable result of ATC’s long-term <strong>scientific partnership, rigorous monitoring, and disciplined grower training</strong>. Our growers aren’t just planting truffle orchards;  they’re <strong>harvesting exceptional truffles</strong>.<br/></p>"
          }
        },
